{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/unicode\/scalar\/utf8view\/enumerated()"]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"enumerated"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18EnumeratedSequenceV","text":"EnumeratedSequence"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"platforms":[{"name":"iOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"iPadOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"Mac Catalyst","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"13.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"macOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"10.10","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"tvOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"9.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"visionOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"1.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"watchOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"2.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","title":"enumerated()","extendedModule":"Swift","externalID":"s:STsE10enumerateds18EnumeratedSequenceVyxGyF::SYNTHESIZED::s:s7UnicodeO6ScalarV8UTF8ViewV","symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Unicode","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Unicode\/Scalar","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Unicode\/Scalar\/UTF8View"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Unicode\/Scalar\/UTF8View\/enumerated()"},"abstract":[{"text":"Returns a sequence of pairs (","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"x"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":"), where ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" represents a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consecutive integer starting at zero and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"x"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" represents an element of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the sequence.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"enumerated","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EnumeratedSequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18EnumeratedSequenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/EnumeratedSequence"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A sequence of pairs enumerating the sequence."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This example enumerates the characters of the string “Swift” and prints"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each character along with its place in the string."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["for (n, c) in \"Swift\".enumerated() {","    print(\"\\(n): '\\(c)'\")","}","\/\/ Prints \"0: 'S'\"","\/\/ Prints \"1: 'w'\"","\/\/ Prints \"2: 'i'\"","\/\/ Prints \"3: 'f'\"","\/\/ Prints \"4: 't'\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When you enumerate a collection, the integer part of each pair is a counter"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for the enumeration, but is not necessarily the index of the paired value."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"These counters can be used as indices only in instances of zero-based,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"integer-indexed collections, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContiguousArray"},{"type":"text","text":". For"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other collections the counters may be out of range or of the wrong type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to use as an index. To iterate over the elements of a collection with its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices, use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"zip(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" function."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This example iterates over the indices and elements of a set, building a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list consisting of indices of names with five or fewer letters."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let names: Set = [\"Sofia\", \"Camilla\", \"Martina\", \"Mateo\", \"Nicolás\"]","var shorterIndices: [Set<String>.Index] = []","for (i, name) in zip(names.indices, names) {","    if name.count <= 5 {","        shorterIndices.append(i)","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now that the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"shorterIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" array holds the indices of the shorter"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"names"},{"type":"text","text":" set, you can use those indices to access elements in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the set."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["for i in shorterIndices {","    print(names[i])","}","\/\/ Prints \"Sofia\"","\/\/ Prints \"Mateo\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"name":"Complexity","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(1)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"}]}],"references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/Unicode":{"title":"Unicode","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A namespace for Unicode utilities."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Unicode","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/unicode","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Unicode","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Unicode","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/Unicode/Scalar":{"title":"Unicode.Scalar","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Unicode scalar value."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Unicode\/Scalar","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/unicode\/scalar","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Scalar","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Scalar","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/EnumeratedSequence":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EnumeratedSequence"}],"title":"EnumeratedSequence","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An enumeration of the elements of a sequence or collection.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/EnumeratedSequence","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EnumeratedSequence"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/enumeratedsequence","kind":"symbol"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/Unicode/Scalar/UTF8View/enumerated()":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"enumerated","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s18EnumeratedSequenceV","text":"EnumeratedSeque